 ```
 
+#### `fullscreen-window-across-monitors`
+
+Toggle the focused window fullscreen across the bounding rectangle of all connected outputs.
+The regular `fullscreen-window` action remains single-output.
+
+```kdl
+binds {
+    Mod+Shift+F { fullscreen-window-across-monitors; }
+}
+```
+
+The action is also available as `niri msg action fullscreen-window-across-monitors`.
+Repeat it to restore the previous window state.
+Changing focus, entering the overview, or changing the output arrangement ends this mode.
+Each output displays its corresponding part of the window; outputs are not mirrored.
+Output positions, rotations, and scales determine the logical bounding rectangle.
+Parts of the window falling into gaps between outputs are not visible.
+Clients are asked to render at the highest scale among the covered outputs.
+
 #### `do-screen-transition`
 
 <sup>Since: 0.1.6</sup>
